      "section_path": [
        "Clock-In / Clock-Out Manual",
        "Register actual time"
      ],
      "text": "Clock-in and clock-out record actual attendance, not merely the published roster. Open My time > Clock and confirm the workplace timezone displayed above the controls. A shift may cross midnight; always inspect both the date and the time. PeopleFlow stores timestamps in UTC and presents them in the workplace timezone. A daylight-saving transition is calculated from elapsed UTC time, not by subtracting displayed local clock labels.",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "heading_level": 2,
      "is_semantic": true,
      "list_level": null,
      "location": {
        "bbox": null,
        "element": 6,
        "line": null,
        "page": null,
        "part": null
      },
      "marker": null,
      "ordered": null,
      "rows": null,
      "section_path": [
        "Clock-In / Clock-Out Manual",
        "Daily procedure"
      ],
      "text": "Daily procedure",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "heading_level": null,
      "is_semantic": true,
      "list_level": 0,
      "location": {
        "bbox": null,
        "element": 8,
        "line": null,
        "page": null,
        "part": null
      },
      "marker": "1.",
      "ordered": true,
      "rows": null,
      "section_path": [
        "Clock-In / Clock-Out Manual",
        "Daily procedure"
      ],
      "text": "Select Clock in when work begins. Confirm that an open attendance session appears.",
      "type": "list_item"
    },
    {
      "heading_level": null,
      "is_semantic": true,
      "list_level": 0,
      "location": {
        "bbox": null,
        "element": 9,
        "line": null,
        "page": null,
        "part": null
      },
      "marker": "2.",
      "ordered": true,
      "rows": null,
      "section_path": [
        "Clock-In / Clock-Out Manual",
        "Daily procedure"
      ],
      "text": "Select Start break when an unpaid break begins, then End break on return.",
      "type": "list_item"
    },
    {
      "heading_level": null,
      "is_semantic": true,
      "list_level": 0,
      "location": {
        "bbox": null,
        "element": 10,
        "line": null,
        "page": null,
        "part": null
      },
      "marker": "3.",
      "ordered": true,
      "rows": null,
      "section_path": [
        "Clock-In / Clock-Out Manual",
        "Daily procedure"
      ],
      "text": "Select Clock out when work ends and review the closed attendance interval.",
      "type": "list_item"
    },
    {
      "heading_level": null,
      "is_semantic": true,
      "list_level": 0,
      "location": {
        "bbox": null,
        "element": 11,
        "line": null,
        "page": null,
        "part": null
      },
      "marker": "4.",
      "ordered": true,
      "rows": null,
      "section_path": [
        "Clock-In / Clock-Out Manual",
        "Daily procedure"
      ],
      "text": "Check the daily total after the next calculation cycle, which runs every five minutes.",
      "type": "list_item"
    },
    {
      "heading_level": null,
      "is_semantic": true,
      "list_level": null,
      "location": {
        "bbox": null,
        "element": 12,
        "line": null,
        "page": null,
        "part": null
      },
      "marker": null,
      "ordered": null,
      "rows": null,
      "section_path": [
        "Clock-In / Clock-Out Manual",
        "Daily procedure"
      ],
      "text": "One open attendance session is allowed per employee. CLOCK-409 means an open session already exists or a repeated clock-out was attempted. It does not mean the first event failed. Refresh the timeline before retrying. CLOCK-422 means event ordering is invalid, such as a break end preceding its start. PeopleFlow does not manufacture a missing clock-out from a roster end time.",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "heading_level": 2,
      "is_semantic": true,
      "list_level": null,
      "location": {
        "bbox": null,
        "element": 13,
        "line": null,
        "page": null,
        "part": null
      },
      "marker": null,
      "ordered": null,
      "rows": null,
      "section_path": [
        "Clock-In / Clock-Out Manual",
        "Breaks and missing events"
      ],
      "text": "Breaks and missing events",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "heading_level": null,
      "is_semantic": true,
      "list_level": null,
      "location": {
        "bbox": null,
        "element": 14,
        "line": null,
        "page": null,
        "part": null
      },
      "marker": null,
      "ordered": null,
      "rows": null,
      "section_path": [
        "Clock-In / Clock-Out Manual",
        "Breaks and missing events"
      ],
      "text": "A 30-minute unpaid break is expected for shifts longer than six hours, but the system deducts recorded breaks only; it does not silently deduct an unrecorded break. A missing break generates a manager review flag. Worked time equals the closed interval minus recorded unpaid breaks. A 09:00-17:30 interval with a 30-minute unpaid break produces 8.00 hours.",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "heading_level": 2,
      "is_semantic": true,
      "list_level": null,
      "location": {
        "bbox": null,
        "element": 15,
        "line": null,
        "page": null,
        "part": null
      },
      "marker": null,
      "ordered": null,
      "rows": null,
      "section_path": [
        "Clock-In / Clock-Out Manual",
        "Corrections and exceptions"
      ],
      "text": "Corrections and exceptions",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "heading_level": null,
      "is_semantic": true,
      "list_level": null,
      "location": {
        "bbox": null,
        "element": 16,
        "line": null,
        "page": null,
        "part": null
      },
      "marker": null,
      "ordered": null,
      "rows": null,
      "section_path": [
        "Clock-In / Clock-Out Manual",
        "Corrections and exceptions"
      ],
      "text": "For current records, use Attendance Correction Guide v2 to submit a self-service correction request. Employees propose corrected values; approval still belongs to the manager. A terminal outage should be documented with the approximate event times and a workplace explanation. Do not enter another clock-in to close an earlier session. If the total remains zero after five minutes despite a closed interval, use Attendance Troubleshooting and include the attendance calculation status in the ticket.",
      "type": "paragraph"
    }
  ],
